mesa-ps4 @ 1a59cc1: VK_EXT_map_memory_placed on the PS4. 32-bit Wine (win32u's WoW64 vkMapMemory2) needs the
extension to get host-visible memory below 4 GiB, but RADV advertised it only with KMS/DRM, and the Orbis
arm's ac_drm_bo_cpu_map refused any requested address, so no 32-bit Vulkan program could map memory (win32u
fell back to RADV's own mapping above 4 GiB and refused it). RADV now advertises the extension on the PS4 as
well (__PS4__), and a requested address gets a CPU-only alias of the BO's physical pages there (the arena's,
or the BO's GARLIC chunk), mapped with MAP_FIXED over what the caller committed; ac_drm_bo_cpu_unmap and BO
free turn the alias back into a reservation (VK_MEMORY_UNMAP_RESERVE_BIT_EXT), and RADV's unmap-with-replace
on the no-DRM arm takes that path for a placed mapping. ac_orbis_drm_alias_stats reports the aliases for the
title (libvulkan.prx: pw_vulkan_alias_stats). Milestone g (docs/ps4/HANDOFF-g.md, gap 1). Applied by
scripts/ps4/build.sh mesa.

